Z||000000||DXR_DAD||01-01-2000||09:35 PM||||Lots of talk of good sunny days. good for washing and waxing are cars, what is the going price at the detail shops nowdays. I like to think that I can do the best job on my own car but would like to see what the pros could do to it and the price.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Ed||01-01-2000||09:56 PM||||The local car wash charges various prices for the different services. The cheapest price I've seen is about $40 for a quick wax.<P>I've had them do my cars a couple of times, but I haven't been impressed. Just get a good polish and a good wax and have at it. If its bad enough to have the pros do it, you probably need a new paint job! ||||reg||1
Z||000002||2FAST4U||01-01-2000||10:10 PM||||Hey Dad;<BR>Wow it's been a long time since I've said that.<BR>Since I have over 20 company cars that are under my controll I use several detail shops here in denver and they all charge about the same $80.00 to $100.00 for a complete in and out detail. While most of them do an adequit job I am never completly happy. I always find something that makes me feel that I could do a better job myself. I still prefer to do my personal cars myself. I guess maby it's a pride of accomplishment thing or something, but I enjoy doing my own cars and then standing back and admiring the accomplishment when I'm finished.<P>Joe||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||01-01-2000||10:42 PM||||I just might give the SE a treat and send her in and get the works in and out, just to see how she comes out. There is a place here that does the city cars, police, fire dept and lots of limos. 2FAST yea, it feels a lot better when you do it yourself and I think I do a dang good job but I would like to see how good they do. If its not too much$$$||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||01-02-2000||02:10 AM||||Most places around here charge any where from $100 up to $175US.  There is one shop I know of that does an OUTSTANDING job and usually has a 2-3 week waiting list.  They charge a flat $150US, but when they get done, you have to look carefully to make sure they didn't replace your car with a brand new one.  They will even touch up small paint chips, and fix small tears in your leather if you ask them to.  Years ago I bought a dirty nasty MGBGT from a boneyard.  The car was complete, but had been sitting in the weather for about a year with one of the windows rolled halfway down.  I bought it for less than $500 and planned to resell it.  As a joke (so I thought) I took it in to get detailed (the shop wasn't too happy).  It came out looking almost new and I got an offer of $1800 the next day.  Quickest $1150 I ever made.  <P>OK. So I got off track a little bit.  I haven't had my medication yet today.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Smokey||01-02-2000||04:10 AM||||I do that for a living, always got a clean car myself :-) It's around $100 for a full detail i believe, but im not sure. I just do the detailing....the bosses decide the price. I have a friend with his own detail shop and he only charges $140 for a full detail on vans! i guess it depends on where you go||||reg||1
